Yuan,

Regarding this error:

On Mon, 2023-09-11 at 06:53 -0700, Yuanyuan Hu wrote:
> Chain 1: Exception: Exception: invese_spd: LDLT factor failed   (in 'model_stanmarg' at line 384)
>   (in 'model_stanmarg' at line 1835)

I recently made an improvement on github so that you should see fewer of these messages. If you only see this during the burnin/warmup period, you should have nothing to worry about. It can happen when the sampler has not yet converged to the posterior distribution and is currently evaluating the model at "bad" parameter values. Though it is also possible after burnin/warmup, possibly due to lack of model convergence or to non-positive definite covariance matrices.

About the model code that you sent: I am not sure that the ":" syntax will work correctly in blavaan. I haven't tested that operator so much, though it might work ok...

Ed

